==Post-match==
[[File:Fullscore.JPG|thumb|The Wembley scoreboard at the final whistle.|alt=An electronic scoreboard at a football ground.]]
After the match, Portsmouth captain Campbell was presented with the trophy by [[Bobby Robson]]. Kanu, the scorer of the winning goal, was named [[Player of the match|man of the match]] and described the win as the "best moment of my life",<ref name="aih"/><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/sport/football/2300733/FA-Cup-final-Kanu-punishes-Cardiff-to-win-Cup.html |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/20220112/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/sport/football/2300733/FA-Cup-final-Kanu-punishes-Cardiff-to-win-Cup.html |archive-date=12 January 2022 |url-access=subscription |url-status=live|title=FA Cup final: Kanu punishes Cardiff to win Cup|newspaper=The Telegraph|last=Collins |first=Roy|date=8 May 2008|access-date=9 February 2020}}{{cbignore}}</ref> while the victory was the first major trophy that manager [[Harry Redknapp]] had won during his 25-year managerial career.<ref name="bbcreport"/> He described it as "dream come true to win the FA Cup. It has been a good day."<ref name="survival">{{cite news |url=https://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/fa_cup/7406516.stm |title=Survival beats Cup win – Redknapp |publisher=BBC Sport |date=17 May 2008 |access-date=3 October 2020}}</ref> The Portsmouth team attended a victory parade in their home city the following day that was attended by around 200,000 people.<ref>{{cite news |url=http://www.bbc.co.uk/hampshire/content/articles/2008/05/15/pompey_victory_parade_feature.shtml |title=Portsmouth Celebrates |work=BBC News |access-date=3 October 2020}}</ref> As winners, Portsmouth also qualified for the [[2008 FA Community Shield]] against Premier League winners Manchester United in August. The two sides played out a goalless draw before United won the tie in a [[penalty shootout]].<ref>{{cite news |url=https://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/7549022.stm |title=Man Utd 0–0 Portsmouth (Man Utd win 3–1 on pens) |publisher=BBC Sport |last=Bevan |first=Chris |date=10 August 2008 |access-date=3 October 2020}}</ref>

Of the 16 players in Portsmouth's matchday squad, the final was the last match for two, Muntari and Baros,<ref name="portswatn">{{cite news |url=https://www.hampshirelive.news/sport/football/football-news/whatever-happened-portsmouths-2008-fa-4205523 |title=Whatever happened to Portsmouth's 2008 FA Cup-winning team |publisher=Hampshire Live |last=Baker |first=Max |date=8 June 2020 |access-date=4 October 2020}}</ref><ref name=signedgalatasaray>{{Cite web|url=https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/transfers/transfer-news-and-speculation-27-august-909537.html |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/20220501/https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/transfers/transfer-news-and-speculation-27-august-909537.html |archive-date=1 May 2022 |url-access=subscription|title=Baros quits France for move to Turkey|newspaper=The Independent|date=27 August 2008|access-date=3 October 2020}}{{cbignore}}</ref> while Mendes appeared in the Community Shield before being sold to [[Rangers F.C.|Rangers]].<ref name="portswatn"/> Redknapp also left the club three months into the new season, taking charge of Tottenham Hotspur.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://uk.reuters.com/article/uk-soccer-england-tottenham-redknapp-fap/tottenham-confirm-redknapp-appointment-idUKTRE49P1J020081026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201120025452/https://uk.reuters.com/article/uk-soccer-england-tottenham-redknapp-fap/tottenham-confirm-redknapp-appointment-idUKTRE49P1J020081026 |url-status=dead |archive-date=20 November 2020 |title=Tottenham confirm Redknapp appointment |publisher=Reuters |last=Herman |first=Martyn |date=26 October 2008 |access-date=4 October 2020}}</ref> Portsmouth reached the final again in [[2010 FA Cup final|2010]] under [[Avram Grant]], losing 1–0 to [[Chelsea F.C.|Chelsea]].<ref>{{cite news |url=https://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/fa_cup/8680493.stm |title=Chelsea 1–0 Portsmouth |publisher=BBC Sport |last=McNulty |first=Phil |date=15 May 2010 |access-date=4 October 2020}}</ref>
 
Jones was pragmatic about his side's defeat, stating "we gave it everything we had and that's all I asked for".<ref name="cardiffquote">{{cite news |url=https://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/fa_cup/7406432.stm |title=Jones proud of beaten Bluebirds |publisher=BBC Sport |date=17 May 2008 |access-date=3 October 2020}}</ref> Enckelman later recalled his error that lead to the only goal "It was a tough one to deal with, it was wet conditions and the ball just started dropping down, maybe I could have tried to catch it or something but I didn't deal with it well enough."<ref name="cardiffquote"/> Despite their defeat, a return party was held for the Cardiff team at [[Roald Dahl Plass]] in [[Cardiff Bay]] in which both Thompson and Fox performed their FA Cup final songs.<ref name="wc173">{{harvnb|Wozencroft|2013|p=173}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/1/hi/wales/7406525.stm |title=Defeated Cardiff team return home |work=BBC News |date=18 May 2008 |access-date=2 October 2020}}</ref> Several players involved in the match for Cardiff left the club prior to the new season, with veteran trio Hasselbaink and Sinclair retiring and Fowler joining [[Blackburn Rovers F.C.|Blackburn Rovers]].<ref name="metro">{{cite news |url=https://metro.co.uk/2014/06/05/cardiff-citys-2008-fa-cup-final-team-where-are-they-now-4748073/ |title=Cardiff City's 2008 FA Cup final team – Where are they now? |newspaper=Metro |last=Gleed |first=Hadyn |date=5 June 2014 |access-date=4 October 2020}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2008/jul/11/Cardiffcity.Blackburn |title=Fowler set for top-flight return at Blackburn |newspaper=The Guardian |date=11 July 2008 |access-date=3 October 2020}}</ref> Loovens, Ramsey and Thompson were also sold during the summer.<ref name="metro"/><ref>{{harvnb|Saunders|2013|p=300}}</ref>

The 2008 final led the FA and the [[English Football League|Football League]] to largely ban the playing of anthems in future matches between English and Welsh sides after jeering from both sets of supporters.<ref name="wc170">{{harvnb|Wozencroft|2013|p=170}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/sport/football/teams/liverpool/9100199/Carling-Cup-final-2012-no-national-anthems-to-be-played-ahead-of-Liverpools-clash-with-Cardiff-City.html |title=Carling Cup final 2012: no national anthems to be played ahead of Liverpool's clash with Cardiff City |newspaper=[[The Daily Telegraph]] |date=23 February 2012 |access-date=27 April 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180427183948/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/sport/football/teams/liverpool/9100199/Carling-Cup-final-2012-no-national-anthems-to-be-played-ahead-of-Liverpools-clash-with-Cardiff-City.html |archive-date=27 April 2018 |url-status=live }}</ref> The 89,874 attendance for the match remains the largest for a football match at the redeveloped Wembley Stadium since its construction.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.cardiffcityfc.co.uk/news/day-2008-fa-cup-final |title=On This Day 2008 FA Cup Final |publisher=Cardiff City F.C. |access-date=4 October 2020}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.goal.com/en-gb/news/when-is-the-fa-cup-2019-20-final-will-fans-be-allowed-to/1dm8o904aii601i2ielgn0or24 |title=When is the FA Cup 2019–20 final & will fans be allowed to attend? |website=goal.com |date=29 July 2020 |access-date=30 December 2020}}</ref>

